====================================================================================
(a) does every trial end high, as a clock would require?
====================================================================================

352 trials. Arousal in the final 3 s before the trial ends.

  all trials  (n = 352)
    mean 58.2, median 63.9, SD 34.9, range 0.0-100.0
    ending below  25:  26.7% of trials
    ending below  50:  40.6% of trials
    ending below  75:  57.7% of trials
    correlation with trial duration: r = +0.290 (p = 3.05e-08)

  hard course  (n = 173)
    mean 51.8, median 56.7, SD 34.6, range 0.0-99.9
    ending below  25:  32.4% of trials
    ending below  50:  48.6% of trials
    ending below  75:  65.3% of trials
    correlation with trial duration: r = +0.225 (p = 0.00289)

  A clock predicts every trial ends near the top of its ramp and that
  final value rises steeply with duration. Compare the spread and the
  duration correlation above against that prediction.

